# Every file in this directory is a deliberately public document — the
# whole point of "well-known" (key discovery, revocation checks, SPEC.md's
# own convention). Every atlas/*.php route already sends
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * via cors_headers(), but a file here is
# served directly by Apache, never through a PHP script, so that never
# runs for it. Invisible in every demo on this site that plays both
# federated roles on one server (same-origin fetch, CORS never applies) —
# only surfaces once a browser genuinely fetches another, separate
# domain's own key cross-origin, which federation-demo.html's independent
# signature verification does. Mirrors issuer-server/server.js's
# serveStatic(), which already sends this header on every static response
# unconditionally.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header always set Access-Control-Allow-Origin "*"
</IfModule>
